{
  "text": "2008A01 An 80 year old woman is\nundergoing major emergency surgery.\nDescribe the maintenance inhaled concentration of sevoflurane you\nwould choose\nand the factors that might influence this.\nList:\n·\nIntro\n·\nPD: age and illness\n·\nEffect of adjuvant opioid\n·\nVolatile kinetics: age and illness\n·\nAnaesthetic and surgical factors\n·\nThe answer\nIntro:\nAims\n·\nEnsure amnesia, hypnosis, immobility\n·\nPrevent awareness (lower risk)\n·\nMinimise CVS toxicity (higher risk)\nProblems\n·\nElderly\n·\nAcutely unwell\n·\nMajor surgery\nMaintenance inhaled concentration\n·\nAfter 15 mins, close to equilibration between inhaled,\nalveolar exhaled partial pressure\n·\nHence consider equivalent to MAC\nPharmacodynamics: age and\nillness\nValues\n·\nMAC-amnesia 0.25\n·\nMAC-awake 0.33\n·\nMAC (immobility) 1.0\nFactors reducing all MAC values\n·\nAge: note quite linear ↓6% per decade after 40yrs\n(at 80: 1.4%)\n·\nSevere illness: mAP<40mmHg, PaO\n2\n<40mmHg,\nPaCO\n2\n>80mmHg, ↓pH,\n↓temp\n·\nAdjuvant drugs: opioids, benzodiazepines\nEffect of adjuvant\nopioid:\nSevo alone\nSevo + fentanyl 3ng/mL\nMACBAR\n4.15%\n↓80%\nMAC\n1.85%\n↓60%\nMACawake (0.3)\n0.6%\n↓25%\nStandard deviation\n0.1\n<0.1\nVolatile pharmacokinetics\nkinetics: age and illness\nAbsorption\n·\n↓Cardiac output -> ↑rate of rise\nF\nA\n/F\nI\nDistribution\n·\n↓Cardiac output (↑age) ->\n↑rate of rise F\nA\n/F\nI\n·\n↓Muscle mass ↑rate of rise\nF\nA\n/F\nI\nMetabolism\n·\n↓Liver enzymatic activity -> ↓rate\nof consumption -> ↑rate of rise\nF\nA\n/F\nI\nExcretion\n·\nN/A\nAnaesthetic and surgical\nfactors:\ne.g. fractured NOF\n·\nSpinal anaesthetic-> ↓nociceptive activation\nof ARAS -> ↓↓MAC requirement\ne.g. laparotomy, thoracotomy\n·\n↑↑Stimulation ->\n↑MAC requirement\nAnswer:\nConsiderations\n·\nVery low risk of awareness at 0.8 MAC = 1.1%\n·\nSignificant reduction in MAC with age, illness,\nadjuvants\n·\nLikely rapid\n↑F\nA\n/F\nI\n·\nHowever need to account for ΔFA/FI\nFinal answer\n·\nInspired\nconcentration\n1.5%\n·\nRecommend EEG monitoring e.g. BIS, aim 40-60\n(I don’t know if this is the\ncorrect answer)\nFeedback welcome at\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
